---@field ApplyMapping? aws.glue.ApplyMapping Specifies a transform that maps data property keys in the data source to data property keys in the data target. You can rename keys, modify the data types for keys, and choose which keys to drop from the dataset.
---@field SelectFields? aws.glue.SelectFields Specifies a transform that chooses the data property keys that you want to keep.
---@field DropFields? aws.glue.DropFields Specifies a transform that chooses the data property keys that you want to drop.
---@field RenameField? aws.glue.RenameField Specifies a transform that renames a single data property key.
---@field Spigot? aws.glue.Spigot Specifies a transform that writes samples of the data to an Amazon S3 bucket.
---@field Join? aws.glue.Join Specifies a transform that joins two datasets into one dataset using a comparison phrase on the specified data property keys. You can use inner, outer, left, right, left semi, and left anti joins.
---@field SplitFields? aws.glue.SplitFields Specifies a transform that splits data property keys into two DynamicFrames. The output is a collection of DynamicFrames: one with selected data property keys, and one with the remaining data property keys.
---@field SelectFromCollection? aws.glue.SelectFromCollection Specifies a transform that chooses one DynamicFrame from a collection of DynamicFrames. The output is the selected DynamicFrame
---@field FillMissingValues? aws.glue.FillMissingValues Specifies a transform that locates records in the dataset that have missing values and adds a new field with a value determined by imputation. The input data set is used to train the machine learning model that determines what the missing value should be.
---@field Filter? aws.glue.Filter Specifies a transform that splits a dataset into two, based on a filter condition.
---@field CustomCode? aws.glue.CustomCode Specifies a transform that uses custom code you provide to perform the data transformation. The output is a collection of DynamicFrames.
---@field SparkSQL? aws.glue.SparkSQL Specifies a transform where you enter a SQL query using Spark SQL syntax to transform the data. The output is a single DynamicFrame.
---@field DirectKinesisSource? aws.glue.DirectKinesisSource Specifies a direct Amazon Kinesis data source.
---@field DirectKafkaSource? aws.glue.DirectKafkaSource Specifies an Apache Kafka data store.
---@field CatalogKinesisSource? aws.glue.CatalogKinesisSource Specifies a Kinesis data source in the Glue Data Catalog.
---@field CatalogKafkaSource? aws.glue.CatalogKafkaSource Specifies an Apache Kafka data store in the Data Catalog.
---@field DropNullFields? aws.glue.DropNullFields Specifies a transform that removes columns from the dataset if all values in the column are 'null'. By default, Glue Studio will recognize null objects, but some values such as empty strings, strings that are "null", -1 integers or other placeholders such as zeros, are not automatically recognized as nulls.
---@field Merge? aws.glue.Merge Specifies a transform that merges a DynamicFrame with a staging DynamicFrame based on the specified primary keys to identify records. Duplicate records (records with the same primary keys) are not de-duplicated.
---@field Union? aws.glue.Union Specifies a transform that combines the rows from two or more datasets into a single result.
---@field PIIDetection? aws.glue.PIIDetection Specifies a transform that identifies, removes or masks PII data.
---@field Aggregate? aws.glue.Aggregate Specifies a transform that groups rows by chosen fields and computes the aggregated value by specified function.
---@field DropDuplicates? aws.glue.DropDuplicates Specifies a transform that removes rows of repeating data from a data set.
---@field GovernedCatalogTarget? aws.glue.GovernedCatalogTarget Specifies a data target that writes to a goverened catalog.
---@field GovernedCatalogSource? aws.glue.GovernedCatalogSource Specifies a data source in a goverened Data Catalog.
