---@field minInputFiles? aws.glue.NullableInteger The minimum number of data files that must be present in a partition before compaction will actually compact files. This parameter helps control when compaction is triggered, preventing unnecessary compaction operations on partitions with few files. If an input is not provided, the default value 100 will be used.
---@field deleteFileThreshold? aws.glue.NullableInteger The minimum number of deletes that must be present in a data file to make it eligible for compaction. This parameter helps optimize compaction by focusing on files that contain a significant number of delete operations, which can improve query performance by removing deleted records. If an input is not provided, the default value 1 will be used.

