---@field Description? aws.glue.DescriptionString The description of the session.
---@field Role? aws.glue.OrchestrationRoleArn The name or Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the IAM role associated with the Session.
---@field Command? aws.glue.SessionCommand The command object.See SessionCommand.
---@field DefaultArguments? aws.glue.OrchestrationArgumentsMap A map array of key-value pairs. Max is 75 pairs.
---@field Connections? aws.glue.ConnectionsList The number of connections used for the session.
---@field Progress aws.glue.DoubleValue The code execution progress of the session.
---@field MaxCapacity? aws.glue.NullableDouble The number of Glue data processing units (DPUs) that can be allocated when the job runs. A DPU is a relative measure of processing power that consists of 4 vCPUs of compute capacity and 16 GB memory.
---@field SecurityConfiguration? aws.glue.NameString The name of the SecurityConfiguration structure to be used with the session.
---@field GlueVersion? aws.glue.GlueVersionString The Glue version determines the versions of Apache Spark and Python that Glue supports. The GlueVersion must be greater than 2.0.
---@field NumberOfWorkers? aws.glue.NullableInteger The number of workers of a defined WorkerType to use for the session.
---@field WorkerType? aws.glue.WorkerType The type of predefined worker that is allocated when a session runs. Accepts a value of G.1X, G.2X, G.4X, G.8X, G.12X, G.16X, R.1X, R.2X, R.4X, or R.8X for Spark sessions. Accepts the value Z.2X for Ray sessions.
---@field CompletedOn? aws.glue.TimestampValue The date and time that this session is completed.
---@field ExecutionTime? aws.glue.NullableDouble The total time the session ran for.
---@field DPUSeconds? aws.glue.NullableDouble The DPUs consumed by the session (formula: ExecutionTime * MaxCapacity).
---@field IdleTimeout? aws.glue.IdleTimeout The number of minutes when idle before the session times out.
---@field ProfileName? aws.glue.NameString The name of an Glue usage profile associated with the session.
---@field SessionType? aws.glue.SessionType The type of the session.

