---Specifies configuration for Snowflake nodes in Glue Studio.
---@class aws.glue.SnowflakeNodeData
---@field SourceType? aws.glue.GenericLimitedString Specifies how retrieved data is specified. Valid values: "table", "query".
---@field Connection? aws.glue.Option Specifies a Glue Data Catalog Connection to a Snowflake endpoint.
---@field Schema? aws.glue.GenericString Specifies a Snowflake database schema for your node to use.
---@field Table? aws.glue.GenericString Specifies a Snowflake table for your node to use.
---@field Database? aws.glue.GenericString Specifies a Snowflake database for your node to use.
---@field TempDir? aws.glue.EnclosedInStringProperty Not currently used.
---@field IamRole? aws.glue.Option Not currently used.
---@field AdditionalOptions? aws.glue.AdditionalOptions Specifies additional options passed to the Snowflake connector. If options are specified elsewhere in this node, this will take precedence.
---@field SampleQuery? aws.glue.GenericString A SQL string used to retrieve data with the query sourcetype.
---@field PreAction? aws.glue.GenericString A SQL string run before the Snowflake connector performs its standard actions.
---@field PostAction? aws.glue.GenericString A SQL string run after the Snowflake connector performs its standard actions.
---@field Action? aws.glue.GenericString Specifies what action to take when writing to a table with preexisting data. Valid values: append, merge, truncate, drop.
---@field Upsert? aws.glue.BooleanValue Used when Action is append. Specifies the resolution behavior when a row already exists. If true, preexisting rows will be updated. If false, those rows will be inserted.
---@field MergeAction? aws.glue.GenericLimitedString Specifies a merge action. Valid values: simple, custom. If simple, merge behavior is defined by MergeWhenMatched and MergeWhenNotMatched. If custom, defined by MergeClause.
---@field MergeWhenMatched? aws.glue.GenericLimitedString Specifies how to resolve records that match preexisting data when merging. Valid values: update, delete.
---@field MergeWhenNotMatched? aws.glue.GenericLimitedString Specifies how to process records that do not match preexisting data when merging. Valid values: insert, none.
---@field MergeClause? aws.glue.GenericString A SQL statement that specifies a custom merge behavior.
---@field StagingTable? aws.glue.GenericString The name of a staging table used when performing merge or upsert append actions. Data is written to this table, then moved to table by a generated postaction.
---@field SelectedColumns? aws.glue.OptionList Specifies the columns combined to identify a record when detecting matches for merges and upserts. A list of structures with value, label and description keys. Each structure describes a column.
---@field AutoPushdown? aws.glue.BooleanValue Specifies whether automatic query pushdown is enabled. If pushdown is enabled, then when a query is run on Spark, if part of the query can be "pushed down" to the Snowflake server, it is pushed down. This improves performance of some queries.
---@field TableSchema? aws.glue.OptionList Manually defines the target schema for the node. A list of structures with value , label and description keys. Each structure defines a column.

